		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4414&amp;p=33710#p33710"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Are you sure you press SK2 + GREEN to permanently store the use location setting ?</div></blockquote>YES. Today I plan to reload the latest CPS and Firmware again one more time just incase there was a issue with the previous uploads.<br><br>Will update finding over the next few days<br><br>Many thanks <br><br>John<br>GW6RTV</div></blockquote>I've checked the operation, and it is working, however it may not appear to be working. On my V2 9600 and my other radios.<br><br><br>I think the problem is that if you change the Location setting, must be saved permanently before it will take any effect.<br><br>And ... exiting from the Channel Details screen is not currently forcing a re-sort of the current zone.  So that even if you save it permanently, you won't see any difference unless you go into the QuickMenu -&gt; Roaming and force a re-sort by pressing enter on the Manual or distance value.<br><br>The reason you need to save this setting permanently for it to have an effect, is that the sorting requires that every channel in the zone needs to be reloaded from the codeplug data to get the Location On/Off setting and the Lat/Long, so the current channel , i.e that you just changed the Location status of;  will not remaing in memory and the temporary change of Location:Yes/No will be lost as each of the other channels is loaded into memory.<br><br>Probably one improvement would be for us to determine if the status of the Location setting has been changed by the operator and force a re-sort of the zone when this has happened, or even perhaps just when the operator has permanently saved a change to the channel details.</div></blockquote>Of course you need to permanently save the location flag and/or coordinates if you want to make the sorting function working, as per design if you temporary save the channel, the changes will be reverted on the first channel change (which the sorting function does).<br>In the latest beta, any change to the location flag or coordinates force the sorting function to be executed, but depending of the current channel you are editing, it could remain selected, but that's right because it depends of that channel position in the sorted list.<br>Try to enable/disable the location flag in, lets say, the first two channels of the sorted list, you will see that it works as expected.<br><br>Cheers.<br>---<br>Daniel<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Sat Oct 26, 2024 5:59 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
