<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>OK.<br><br>I've made the changes for the beep and also turning on the backlight<br><br>I decided not to use 1km radius, as this would probably cause the channel to change too frequently.  However I can change this in the future if there is a good reason for a 1km raduis setting<br><br>The new version is here<br><br><a href="https://www.opengd77.com/downloads/MD9600/Firmware/2b33a4d7d7aa782bd5c2599443651f541f9af721" class="postlink">downloads/MD9600/Firmware/2b33a4d7d7aa7 ... 541f9af721</a></div></blockquote>Having uploaded the latest firmware, I can confirm the V2 version works perfectly, even noticed when driving around over the last couple of days while having a cluster zone selected (Group of repeaters linked) that the repeater change over when in use was perfect, the backlight confirmed the switch over to the next nearest repeater, and also the Audable did not overide the speach, therefore no break in the receive transmission.<br>This latest upgrade to the OpenGD77 firmware has taken it to another level.<br><br>John<br>GW6RTV</div></blockquote>Thanks for testing.<br><br>We are working on a few more changes, but nothing drastic, and will hopefully do a full public release at the weekend for all radios.<br>i.e it will also work on the UV380/RT-3S which have GPS fitted, or for that matter a GD77 if people have modified it to include a GPS<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Oct 01, 2024 9:50 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
